{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "title": "MLView public-repository corpus",
  "recorded": "2026-09-14",
  "note": [
    "Thirty-seven real, popular Python ML/DL repositories, pinned to the exact commit",
    "that was analysed: twenty-four recorded on 2026-09-13 (hardening round 1) and",
    "thirteen added on 2026-09-14 (round 2) for framework and domain shapes round 1",
    "never reached - gradient boosting (xgboost, LightGBM), classical statistics and",
    "time series (statsmodels), the accelerate/peft/trl fine-tuning stack, per-trial",
    "HPO objectives (optuna-examples), single-file RL (cleanrl), the official PyTorch",
    "tutorials, a registry/config framework (mmdetection), a hand-written GPT",
    "(LLMs-from-scratch), YAML-driven LLM recipes (torchtune) and a second notebook",
    "book (handson-ml3).",
    "",
    "Nothing here is vendored: this file records a URL, a commit SHA and a",
    "sparse-checkout path list, and `tools/public_corpus.py fetch` clones them into",
    "MLVIEW_PUBLIC_CORPUS_DIR (default `.public-corpus/`, which is NOT part of the",
    "repository). MLView only reads source with `ast`, so a clone is a read, never a",
    "redistribution - but two entries are deliberately not permissively licensed",
    "(`yolov5` is AGPL-3.0, `stable-diffusion` is CreativeML Open RAIL-M) and one",
    "carries no LICENSE file at this SHA (`wandb-examples`). They stay in the corpus",
    "because they are what people actually point an analyzer at; `redistribute: false`",
    "marks every entry whose source must never be copied into this tree or into a",
    "build artefact."
  ],
